      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Somers Point was once known as Somerset Plantation, Somers Ferry, and Somers Plantation before adopting its current name in 1750.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somers_Point%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Somers Point’s maritime past thrives in its fishing, shipbuilding legacy, marinas, and the Somers Mansion—built 1720‑1726 and the county’s oldest house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
